<cell>Match each pair of inequalities with the graph 
of the polar region it describes.
<ol>
<li>
<m>0 \leq r \leq 2</m> and <m>-\pi/2 \leq \theta \leq 3\pi/4</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>2 \leq r \leq 3</m> and <m>\pi/2 \leq \theta \leq 3\pi/2</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>2 \leq r \leq 3</m> and <m>0 \leq \theta \leq 2\pi</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>0 \leq r \leq 2</m> and <m>0 \leq \theta \leq 3\pi/4</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>0 \leq r \leq 3</m> and <m>3\pi/2 \leq \theta \leq 2\pi</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>2 \leq r \leq 3</m> and <m>-\pi/2 \leq \theta \leq \pi/2</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>0 \leq r \leq 2</m> and <m>3\pi/4 \leq \theta \leq 3\pi/2</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>0 \leq r \leq 2</m> and <m>0 \leq \theta \leq 2\pi</m>
</li>
</ol></cell>
